	a <http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#Geometry> .
<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/anarhynchus-frontalis> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A small grey and white plover with a bill that bends to the right, the only bird in the world with a sideways-curved bill. It breeds on the braided gravel riverbeds of Canterbury and Otago in spring and summer, and feeds by sweeping the bill under stones for insect larvae. After breeding, most birds fly north to the harbours of the Firth of Thames and Kaipara, where flocks wheel in tight formation over the tidal flats."@en ;
