<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/anarhynchus-bicinctus/range-centroid> <http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#asWKT> "POINT(171.520 -41.810)"^^<http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#wktLiteral> ;
	a <http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#Geometry> .
<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/anarhynchus-bicinctus> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A small plover of beaches and riverbeds. In the breeding season the adult has a narrow black band across the neck and a broad chestnut band across the breast. It breeds throughout New Zealand. After breeding, many birds from the South Island cross the Tasman Sea to winter in south-eastern Australia, which makes it a rare east-to-west migrant across that sea."@en ;
