<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/anthornis-melanura> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "An olive-green honeyeater whose clear, bell-like song is a well-known sound of New Zealand forests. Captain Cook's crew described the dawn chorus of bellbirds as sounding like small bells. It feeds on nectar, fruit and insects, and lives in forest, scrub and gardens on both main islands."@en ;
