<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/rhipidura-fuliginosa> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A small, restless flycatcher that fans its long tail and follows walkers to catch the insects they disturb. Most birds are grey-brown with a buff belly, but a black form is common in the South Island. It lives in forest, scrub and gardens throughout New Zealand. The grey fantail of Australia, once treated as the same species, is now a separate species."@en ;
