<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/himantopus-leucocephalus> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A black and white wader with very long pink legs and a thin black bill. It feeds by picking insects and small crustaceans from shallow water and wet mud. It breeds in wetlands, riverbeds and pasture throughout New Zealand and Australia. It hybridises with the critically endangered black stilt in the Mackenzie Basin."@en ;
