<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/himantopus-novaezelandiae> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A stilt with entirely black plumage and long red legs, one of the rarest wading birds in the world. It breeds on the braided rivers and wetlands of the Mackenzie Basin. Predators, habitat loss and hybridisation with the pied stilt reduced the wild population to a few dozen birds. A captive breeding programme now releases young birds every year."@en ;
