<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/zosterops-lateralis> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A small olive-green bird with a ring of white feathers around each eye. It colonised New Zealand from Australia in the 1850s without human help, and is now one of the most common birds there. In winter, flocks feed on fruit, nectar and the fat that people put out in gardens."@en ;
