<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/tadorna-variegata> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A large goose-like duck. The female has a white head and the male is almost black, which is unusual among ducks. Pairs stay together for life, and both call loudly when disturbed. It grazes on pasture and short grass and has become more common since farms replaced forest."@en ;
