<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/hymenolaimus-malacorhynchos> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A blue-grey duck of fast, clear mountain rivers, with a pale pink bill and a chestnut-speckled breast. It feeds on insect larvae that it scrapes from rocks in the current. The male's whistle, 'whio', gives the bird its Māori name. Stoats take its eggs and nesting females, so it survives best where traps are set."@en ;
