<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/limosa-lapponica> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A large wader with a long, slightly upturned bill. Birds of the Alaskan population make the longest known non-stop flight of any land bird: from Alaska across the Pacific to New Zealand in about nine days. In spring they fly north to the Yellow Sea, refuel on its tidal flats, then continue to Alaska to breed."@en ;
