<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/calidris-canutus> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A stocky, medium-sized sandpiper, grey in the non-breeding season and brick-red in breeding plumage. It breeds in the high Arctic and migrates in large flocks to coasts in the southern hemisphere. Each flyway depends on a few staging sites: the Yellow Sea for birds that winter in Australia and New Zealand, and Delaware Bay for birds that winter in South America."@en ;
