<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/dacelo-novaeguineae> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A large, stocky kingfisher of eastern Australia, best known for its loud laughing call, which family groups give together at dawn and dusk. It does not need water to hunt: it watches from a perch and drops onto snakes, lizards, insects and small mammals. Young birds from earlier broods help their parents to raise new chicks."@en ;
