<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/dromaius-novaehollandiae> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "The tallest bird in Australia, flightless, with shaggy grey-brown feathers and long legs that can carry it at 50 km/h. It wanders widely across the inland in search of fruit, seeds and insects, and follows rain. The male incubates the eggs for about eight weeks without eating, then cares for the striped chicks for months."@en ;
