<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/eolophus-roseicapilla> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A pink and grey cockatoo that is common across most of Australia. Flocks feed on grass seeds on the ground and in farm paddocks, and have spread with agriculture into cities. Pairs often stay together for life. Birds are known for acrobatics on power lines and in the rain."@en ;
