<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/merops-ornatus> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A slim bee-eater with bright green, blue and gold plumage, a black eye-stripe and long central tail feathers. It catches bees, dragonflies and other flying insects in the air. It nests in tunnels that it digs in sandy banks. Birds from southern Australia migrate north to northern Australia, New Guinea and Indonesia for the winter."@en ;
