<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/numenius-madagascariensis> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "The largest wader in the world, with a very long, down-curved bill that it uses to pull crabs and worms from deep burrows in mudflats. It breeds in north-eastern Asia and spends the non-breeding season on coasts of Australia. The loss of tidal flats in the Yellow Sea, where it stops on migration, has caused a steep decline."@en ;
