<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/calidris-ruficollis> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A sparrow-sized sandpiper, the smallest common wader in Australia. In breeding plumage the face and neck are rufous. It breeds in north-eastern Siberia and western Alaska and flies more than 10,000 km each way to the coasts of Australia, where large flocks feed on the mudflats with fast, short steps."@en ;
