<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/menura-novaehollandiae> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A large, pheasant-like songbird of the moist forests of south-eastern Australia. The male has a long tail of lace-like feathers that he spreads over his head when he displays on a mound of earth. Both sexes are skilled mimics and copy the songs of many forest birds, and sometimes sounds made by people."@en ;
