<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/aquila-audax> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "The largest bird of prey in Australia, dark brown to black, with a long wedge-shaped tail and a wingspan of more than two metres. It soars for hours on thermals over open country. It hunts rabbits, wallabies and birds, and eats carrion, often at roadkill. Pairs build large stick nests that they use for many years."@en ;
