<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/anthochaera-phrygia> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A black and yellow honeyeater with a scaled pattern on the breast and bare pink skin around the eye. It follows the flowering of eucalypts across south-eastern Australia. So few birds are left that young males no longer hear enough adults to learn the correct song, and some sing the songs of other species."@en ;
