<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/calidris-pygmaea> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A small sandpiper with a bill that widens at the tip into a spoon. It breeds only on the coastal tundra of Chukotka in the Russian Far East and winters on mudflats in Bangladesh, Myanmar and southern China. Only a few hundred pairs remain. A conservation programme hatches eggs in captivity and releases the young birds at the breeding grounds."@en ;
