<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/grus-japonensis> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A tall white crane with black wings and neck and a red patch of bare skin on the crown. Pairs perform dances of leaps, bows and calls, which have made the bird a symbol of long life and fidelity in East Asia. A resident population in eastern Hokkaido survives because farmers began to feed it in winter in the 1950s."@en ;
