<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/zosterops-japonicus> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A small olive-green bird with a white ring around each eye. It lives in woodland, parks and gardens in Japan, Korea and eastern China, and feeds on nectar, fruit and insects. In late winter it feeds on the nectar of plum and camellia flowers. It was introduced to Hawaii in 1929 and is now common there."@en ;
