<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/ciconia-boyciana> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A large white stork with black flight feathers, a heavy black bill and red skin around the eye. It breeds in the Amur and Ussuri river basins of the Russian Far East and north-eastern China, and winters in the Yangtze valley. It became extinct in the wild in Japan and Korea, and reintroduced birds now breed again at Toyooka in Japan."@en ;
