<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/hirundo-rustica> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A swallow with glossy blue upperparts, a red throat and long tail streamers. It is the most widespread swallow in the world and breeds across the northern hemisphere, often in barns and sheds. European birds winter in Africa south of the Sahara, and birds ringed in Britain are regularly found in South Africa."@en ;
