<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/cuculus-canorus> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A grey, hawk-like cuckoo whose two-note call announces spring across Europe. The female lays single eggs in the nests of reed warblers, meadow pipits and other small birds, and each female line specialises in one host. Adults leave for central Africa in summer, and the young birds find their way there alone weeks later."@en ;
