<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/apus-apus> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A dark, sickle-winged bird that spends almost its whole life in the air. It feeds, drinks, sleeps and mates on the wing, and a young bird may not land for two or three years after it leaves the nest. It nests in holes in old buildings across Europe, arrives in May and leaves in August for Africa south of the equator."@en ;
