<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/ciconia-ciconia> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A tall white stork with black flight feathers and a red bill and legs. It nests on roofs, church towers and electricity pylons, and pairs greet each other by clattering their bills. Migrants avoid long sea crossings and soar on thermals over the Strait of Gibraltar or the Bosphorus. Many Iberian birds now stay all winter and feed at rubbish tips."@en ;
