<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/sterna-paradisaea> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A slender, grey and white tern with a black cap and a blood-red bill. It breeds around the Arctic and spends the northern winter in the Southern Ocean near Antarctica, so it sees more daylight than any other animal. Tracking has shown that some birds fly more than 90,000 km in a year."@en ;
