<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/upupa-epops> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A pinkish-brown bird with a long, thin curved bill, black and white barred wings and a crest that it raises like a fan. Its soft call, 'oop-oop-oop', gives the bird its name in many languages. It probes the ground for insect larvae. Birds from Europe winter in Africa south of the Sahara."@en ;
