<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/merops-apiaster> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A colourful bee-eater with a chestnut crown and back, a yellow throat and a turquoise breast. It catches bees and wasps in flight and removes the sting by beating them against a perch. It nests in colonies, in tunnels in sandy banks, across southern Europe, and winters in Africa."@en ;
