<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/vanellus-vanellus> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A black and white plover with green and purple gloss on the back and a long, thin crest. In spring the male performs a tumbling display flight over farmland and calls 'pee-wit'. Its numbers on farmland in Britain have fallen by more than half since the 1980s as farming practices changed."@en ;
