<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/sturnus-vulgaris> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A stocky bird with glossy, spotted black plumage that shines purple and green. It is a skilled mimic. In autumn and winter, roosts of hundreds of thousands of birds form swirling flocks called murmurations. Introductions have made it one of the most widespread birds in the world, including in North America, Australia and New Zealand."@en ;
