<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/phylloscopus-trochilus> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A small, plain olive-green warbler with a pale eyebrow and pale legs. Its sweet, falling song is one of the commonest sounds of spring in northern European woodland. It weighs about 9 g, but birds from Siberia fly up to 12,000 km to winter in eastern and southern Africa."@en ;
