	a <http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#Geometry> .
<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/ficedula-hypoleuca> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A small flycatcher. The breeding male is black and white with a white wing patch, and the female is brown. It nests in holes in oak woodland and readily uses nest boxes. It winters in West Africa. Because it arrives back at a fixed date, warmer springs have caused it to miss the peak of caterpillars in some regions."@en ;
