<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/himantopus-himantopus> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A slim black and white wader with very long pink legs. It breeds in wetlands, salt pans and rice fields in southern Europe, Africa and Asia. European birds winter in Africa. The name Himantopus himantopus once included the stilts of Australia, New Zealand and the Americas, which are now separate species."@en ;
