<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/pandion-haliaetus> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A large fish-eating bird of prey, white below and dark brown above, with a dark stripe through the eye. It dives feet first into water and carries fish head forward in its talons. It occurs on every continent except Antarctica, and northern birds migrate long distances to the tropics."@en ;
