<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/gyps-africanus> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A brown vulture of African savanna with a white rump and a bare dark neck. Flocks find carcasses by watching other vultures from great heights. Poisoned carcasses set out for predators, and poisoning by poachers who do not want circling vultures to reveal their kills, have caused a fall of more than 90 % in three generations."@en ;
