<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/chrysococcyx-caprius> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A small cuckoo. The male is glossy green with white spots on the wing and a red eye, and its call 'dee-dee-dee-deederik' gives the bird its name. It lays its eggs in the nests of weavers and bishops. Southern African birds move north to central Africa in the dry season."@en ;
