<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/archilochus-colubris> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A tiny hummingbird. The male has a ruby-red throat that looks black in poor light. It is the only hummingbird that breeds widely in eastern North America. Before autumn migration it nearly doubles its weight with fat, which lets many birds cross the Gulf of Mexico in one non-stop flight of about 800 km."@en ;
