<https://example.org/birds/vocab/taxon/limosa-haemastica> <https://example.org/birds/def/account> "A large godwit with a long, slightly upturned bill. In breeding plumage it is dark chestnut below. It breeds in Alaska and Canada and flies non-stop over the Atlantic Ocean to winter in southern South America, mainly on the island of Chiloé in Chile and in Tierra del Fuego. In spring it returns through the Great Plains."@en ;
